  "summary": "Several studies directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to the task of estimating agricultural yield. Gupta et al. (2024) report the highest accuracy of 0.89 on the CellLife dataset [V0039]. Fischer et al. (2023) achieve an F1 score of 0.82 using LedgerGuard [V0038], while Haddad et al. (2025) report an MAE of 0.61 on ToxiBench [V0040]. El-Sayed et al. (2022) apply the method to AgriSat-4, achieving an AUROC of 0.75 [V0037]. For comparison, a non-gradient-boosting approach using message passing over relational graphs on AgriSat-4 yielded an F1 score of 0.77 [V0025].",
